{"path":"chrono/c/timespec_get","title":"std::timespec_get","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>timespec_get","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec_get","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"Other macro constants beginning with TIME_ may be provided by the implementation to indicate additional time bases.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ctime\">&lt;ctime&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> timespec_get<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec\"><span class=\"kw1031\">std::<span class=\"me2\">timespec</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> ts, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> base <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"co2\">#define TIME_UTC /* implementation-defined */</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Modifies the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec\">std::timespec</a></span> object pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ts</span></code> to hold the current calendar time in the time base <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Expands to a value suitable for use as the <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> argument of <code>std::timespec_get</code>.</div>\n<p>Other macro constants beginning with <code>TIME_</code> may be provided by the implementation to indicate additional time bases.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> is <code>TIME_UTC</code>, then\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ts<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>tv_sec</span></code> is set to the number of seconds since an implementation defined epoch, truncated to a whole value,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ts<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>tv_nsec</span></code> member is set to the integral number of nanoseconds, rounded to the resolution of the system clock.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ts\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to an object of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec\">std::timespec</a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> base\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> <code>TIME_UTC</code> or another nonzero integer value indicating the time base\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> if successful, zero otherwise.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The POSIX function <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/clock_getres.html\" data-external=\"1\"><code>clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, ts)</code></a> may also be used to populate a <code>std::timespec</code> with the time since the Epoch.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ctime&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec\"><span class=\"kw1031\">std::<span class=\"me2\">timespec</span></span></a> ts<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">timespec_get</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>ts, TIME_UTC<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> buf<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">100</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/strftime\"><span class=\"kw1022\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strftime</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>buf, sizeof buf, <span class=\"st0\">\"%D&nbsp;%T\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/gmtime\"><span class=\"kw1024\">std::<span class=\"me2\">gmtime</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>ts.<span class=\"me1\">tv_sec</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1773\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Current time: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> buf <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'.'</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> ts.<span class=\"me1\">tv_nsec</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" UTC<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Current time: 06/24/16 20:07:42.949494132 UTC</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/timespec\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>timespec</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> time in seconds and nanoseconds<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(struct)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/time\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>time</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the current time of the system as time since epoch <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/chrono/timespec_get\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>timespec_get</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/c","title":"C Date and time utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::timespec_get","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++17. Modifies the std::timespec object pointed to by ts to hold the current calendar time in the time base base."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"ts, base"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The value of base if successful, zero otherwise."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The POSIX function clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, ts) may also be used to populate a std::timespec with the time since the Epoch."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"timespec","note":"time in seconds and nanoseconds"},{"label":"time","note":"returns the current time of the system as time since epoch"}]}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":233,"codeBlockCount":2}
